 "prior_reconciliation_record": {
  "path": "notes/reconciliation/bn160625945.md (2026-07-22 -> 07-24; read, untouched)",
  "verdict_condensed": "P5: blk11 EXPLAINED - a valid two-break was recovered (DSBPL AIC 2038.4 vs SBPLfree 2062.5, delta = +24.1, xp = 534 keV vs Ravasio's Ep = 673 keV) once the production seed-railing was fixed; Ravasio's fixed smoothness was NOT required (L7). blk15 (207.85-219.75 s) is INCOMPARABLE - past Ravasio's 207.91 s cutoff - and prefers a single break there. Unreconciled secondaries: our E_break ~366 keV vs their 108 keV, and alpha2 ~ -2.0 vs -1.50.",
  "note": "That record's block numbering belongs to the v3 clean_blocks_lle_v2 era and does NOT map onto the 50-block human-final table frozen above. Do not cross-index block numbers between the two."
 },
 "published_frame_at_freeze": {
  "note": "Recorded so the P3 diff cannot be assembled after the fact. Full detail with quotes: results/gcn/bn160625945/bn160625945_dossier.md section 6.",
  "Ravasio_2018": "2SBPL over 186.40-207.91 s: E_break=107.8+/-1.9 keV, Ep=673.5+/-10.8 keV, a1=-0.62, a2=-1.50; >8 sigma over SBPL; 2SBPL FAVOURED OVER SBPL+BB; time-resolved 2SBPL beats SBPL at >4.8 sigma in 19/21 bins; LLE cutoff E_cut=50.3(+7.4/-13.2) MeV",
  "Zhang_2018": "sub-burst 2 (main, 71 slices) = Band / physical synchrotron; thermal component explicitly NOT required ('Adding an additional thermal component neither improves the goodness of the fit...')",
  "Lu_2017": "Episode II (main) = mBB + CPL; a thermal component IS required",
  "Wang_2017": "thermal components in SOME time-resolved intervals + a significant tens-of-MeV cutoff, which they attribute to particle acceleration rather than gamma-gamma",
  "Aldowma_2026_NEWEST": "188.451-214 s GBM+LAT+LLE = ISSM+PL (Ep=755+/-8 keV, dBIC 4); PEAK 188.45-189.47 s GBM+LLE = DSBPL+BB (Ep=2000+/-140 keV, kT=20+/-1.1 keV, dBIC 72). GBM-only twins: Ep=740 keV, and Ep=1680 keV with kT=20 keV, dBIC 76.",
  "Konus_GCN19604": "main 180.480-229.632 s Band: a=-0.79+/-0.02, b=-2.25+/-0.04, Ep=554(-19/+20) keV; peak 256 ms from 188.928 s: Ep=937(-179/+195) keV",
  "GBM_GCN19587": "main 187.427-212.003 s Band: Ep=657+/-5 keV, a=-0.74, b=(-)2.36 (sign typo in the circular)",
  "vonKienlin_2020": "T90 = 453.385+/-0.572 s (50-300 keV) starting T0+188.451 s; T50 = 12.032+/-0.362 s from T0+192.291 s; dets 6+7+9"
 },
 "predictions": [
  "P-A (TWO-BREAK, falsifiable): the blind sweep will find a VALID two-break (DSBPL) winner in a MAJORITY of the bright main-episode blocks between ~188.4 and ~196.7 s, with the DSBPL peak energy XP landing in 500-2500 keV and the break XB in 130-450 keV. FALSIFIED if fewer than half of those blocks return a valid DSBPL with LRT_DSBPL_SBPL >= 9.2, or if XP systematically rails at a bound. Anchor: the archival table already gives 13 significant-and-valid DSBPL blocks and a DSBPL time-integrated winner; Ravasio+2018 and Aldowma+2026 both find two breaks independently. The L8/L9 fixes should INCREASE the count, never decrease it.",
  "P-B (BLACKBODY, falsifiable, and this is the contested one): the blind sweep will fire the union BB rule in 15-30 of the ~50 main-episode blocks, with union kT mostly in the 30-120 keV range. FALSIFIED if the count drops below ~8 or if kT collapses to <10 keV across the board. CRUCIAL DISCRIMINATOR: whether the CPL-arm and Band-arm tallies STILL disagree by ~4-8 blocks. If they do, the 'BB detection' on this burst is baseline-dependent (T8) and CANNOT be quoted as a photosphere - which would side with Ravasio+2018 (2SBPL beats SBPL+BB) and Zhang+2018 (no thermal) against Lu+2017 and Aldowma+2026, and would demonstrate that a two-break continuum and a BB are absorbing the same curvature (L25).",
  "P-C (BREAK-ENERGY OFFSET, falsifiable): our DSBPL break XB will again come out ~2-4x higher than Ravasio+2018's E_break = 107.8 keV (archival integrated: 230 keV; 2026-07-24 blk11: 366 keV). FALSIFIED if the blind XB lands within ~30% of 108 keV. If it survives, the offset is a METHOD difference (binning resolution, interval, LAT/LLE inclusion, or their FIXED smoothness n1=5.38) and must be chased in P4, not written off.",
  "P-D (HIGH-ENERGY CUTOFF, falsifiable): no valid exponential-cutoff winner will be found in the LAT-bearing blocks, i.e. our engine will not reproduce Ravasio's 50 MeV or Wang+2017's tens-of-MeV cutoff. FALSIFIED if a cutoff model wins with a VALID, non-railed E_cut and the cutoff energy sits below the highest LAT photon energy in that block. The prior run's cutoffs railed (L3/L4: photon-starved LAT bins); the EC-vs-max-LAT-photon validity gate is the check that matters.",
  "P-E (PRECURSOR ABSENT, structural): nothing precursor-like will appear, because the precursor is 180 s outside the window. Any 'thermal precursor' result the literature reports (Zhang+2018 sub-burst 1, Lu+2017 Episode I, Konus GCN 19604) is NOT a prediction about our blocks and must never be diffed against them."
 ],
 "traps_carried_forward": [
  "T9 component coverage: T90 = 453 s (von Kienlin, main+extended), 35.1 s (Zhang sub-burst 2), 20.0 +/- 0.4 s (CALET main), 0.8 +/- 0.1 s (CALET precursor) are ALL correct and describe different component sets. Never diff them.",
  "T3/L21 Aldowma alpha ordering: their DSBPL a1 = -1.57 / a2 = -0.66 for the peak interval is the REVERSE of Ravasio's a1 = -0.62 / a2 = -1.50 ordering. Unresolved. Settle at the primary source before diffing any index.",
  "T5 Aldowma cite the DSBPL as Ravasio 2019 in the text and Ravasio 2018 in the appendix.",
  "T7 every 'BB required' / 'BB not required' verdict on this burst is continuum-relative: Ravasio measured against 2SBPL, Zhang against Band+synchrotron, Lu against CPL, Aldowma against DSBPL.",
  "T8 Aldowma report BIC; our engine reports AIC. Do not compare margins without recomputing.",
  "D1 the LLE DRM is single-matrix, built for T0+185.0-202.0 s while the source window is T0+182.644-225.884 s. It PASSES the off-axis test (Delta-theta 1.33 deg mean, 5.23 deg full span) but only because Fermi's ARR slew (42 deg -> 11 deg) FINISHED before both intervals. This is the closest a passing burst gets to the bn130427324 failure."
 ]
